Proprietary, not open source. Source is viewable; viewing grants no rights beyond this license.
Applies from version 0.8.0. Versions up to and including 0.7.0, and all states of the public
repository up to commit 1c079e1 (2026-10-27), were released under the MIT License and remain
under it for anyone who obtains them, also after 0.8.0. Files published unchanged in 0.7.0 stay
under MIT in that form; all changes since 0.7.0 are under this license only.

Without a license code you may install and run the software, including commercially and
internally. Free: the MCP chaos proxy with scenarios F1 to F5, doctor (summary and risk level
of the schema inspection), the compact and plain-language report (without text blocks), the
JSON report, the Resilience Score, the PASS/FAIL/NOT_TESTED verdict and exit code, the
self-test (benchmark) and the demo server. The run is never altered or weakened; verdict, score
and exit code are the same with and without a code. Without a valid code the output of the Pro
scope is shortened or the command is not run.

A valid license code is required for the Pro scope: the full audit dossier, the guided web
interface (ui), the schema assessment with findings and suggestions, the prompt text blocks and
the campaign runner. Licenses ("Harness Pro 90 days", "Harness Pro monthly") cover one system
(an MCP server you test). The code is verified offline and cannot be revoked technically; your
right ends on expiry, termination, refund or chargeback, and you stop using the code. Reports
you created may be kept and passed on unchanged.

The software executes your agent's write operations for real against the connected upstream.
Use it only against a test system with synthetic data that is isolated from third parties and
production; --allow-writes confirms this. Provided "as is". Liability: free use only for intent
and gross negligence; paid licenses: slight negligence excluded, otherwise capped; mandatory
liability remains. You indemnify CuonzTech for use against these terms.

You may not copy, sell, redistribute, sublicense or offer the software as your own product or
service, or remove, bypass or forge license checks or codes. Swiss law applies; exclusive place
of jurisdiction is Thusis, canton of Graubünden, unless mandatory law provides otherwise. Paid
licenses are sold to businesses only. Contact: support@cuonztech.ch
